  PATH          Sets the directories searched for programs
  PAUSE         Waits for a key in a batch file
  PROMPT        Sets the command prompt
  RD            Removes an empty directory
  REM           Marks a comment in a batch file or CONFIG.SYS
  REN           Renames files
  SET           Shows, sets or removes environment variables
  SHIFT         Moves a batch file's parameters down by one
  TIME          Shows or sets the time
  TRUENAME      Shows the full name DOS uses for a file or directory
  TYPE          Shows the contents of a text file
  VER           Shows the DOS version
  VERIFY        Sets whether DOS checks what it writes to disk
  VOL           Shows a disk's volume label and serial number

CONFIG.SYS
  CONFIG        CONFIG.SYS, the settings DOS reads when it starts
  COUNTRY       COUNTRY= in CONFIG.SYS: date, time, number and currency
                 formats

Device drivers and data files
  DISPLAY.SYS   Code page switching for an EGA, VGA or PC Convertible screen
  PRINTER.SYS   Code page switching for IBM printers on LPT1 to LPT3

 INDEX  Line 81/104  WRAP  (END)  Q quit
